  "notes": "USAGE: {貸与|たいよ} is a formal word for lending, used in institutional and official contexts. It implies a temporary provision with the expectation of return, unlike {贈与|ぞうよ} (gift, grant).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {貸与|たいよ}する: to lend, to provide on loan\n- {貸与|たいよ}される: to be provided on loan\n- {貸与|たいよ}{型|がた}{奨学金|しょうがくきん}: loan-type scholarship\n- {貸与|たいよ}{品|ひん}: loaned item, company-provided equipment\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {貸与|たいよ}: lending (formal, institutional)\n- {貸|か}し{出|だ}し: lending, checkout (library or equipment)\n- {融資|ゆうし}: financing, loan (monetary, from a bank)",
